	(text "Latch servo interface - Hiwonder HTS-30HS serial bus servo"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5b85c52c-6026-4ed2-80ce-1b8b9c31164b")
	)
	(text "HTS-30HS: 9-12.6 V (rated 11.1 V), 100 mA no-load, 3.2 A stall, half-duplex UART 115200 baud, packets start 0x55 0x55.\nPower: a full 4S LiFePO4 is 14.6 V, above the servo's 12.6 V maximum, so J17 pin 2 feeds an EXTERNAL buck module\nset to 11.1-12 V (rated 5 A or more). Its output and GND go to the servo plug; SERVO_SIG goes straight to the plug.\nDo not also tie the buck or servo ground to the battery or chassis: the servo current must return only through J17 pin 1.\n\nSignal: PB10 = USART3_TX (AF4) in single-wire half-duplex mode (HDSEL), configured open-drain with R39 pull-up.\nPB11 = SERVO_DIR: drive high just before sending, low as soon as the last byte's TC flag sets (the servo answers\nread commands immediately). U8 translates 3.3 V <-> 5 V; Hiwonder's reference bus has a 10k pull-up to 5 V (R41).\nFirmware note: in half-duplex mode the USART also receives its own transmitted bytes; discard them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "794c5719-82fc-4c81-8330-41ca08da2be1")
	)
